            <ArticleTitle>Squamous carcinoma of the lung metastases to the patella.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>504-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/RLU.0000000000000700</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of a 65-year-old man with newly diagnosed squamous carcinoma of the lung, who presented with worsening left-knee pain. A bone scintigraphy displayed an increased radioactivity in the left patella. The patient underwent left patellectomy. Histopathological examination revealed metastasis to the patella from the known lung cancer.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
